# @song — the family root for the substrate's temporal-progression
# discipline: the typed time-ordered path through a state space that
# discharges cadence at close. Sibling to @mirror (form), @kintsugi
# (process), @loop (endomorphism at type altitude), and @third (marker
# for recursive depth). Arc 6 TICK 1 landing per Seam pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-pre-review-song-substrate-decl.md`
# (RATIFY-WITH-CORRECTIONS on Shape β) against Mara's deep-dive spec
# `docs/specs/song-substrate-decl-v0.1.md` §5.
#
# Alex's direction (2026-07-06 via Reed): `@song` as top-level
# abstraction that binds music-math (`@epistemologic/math/music`
# family) + wire-narrative (`@io/stagefreight/narrative` +
# `@docblock`) + kintsugi-pipeline (`@kintsugi/oscillate` +
# `@kintsugi/shift` + StageFreight cascade) + psychohistory (OBC /
# ADO / regulation stock / extraction / silence / glue work from
# Alex's `systemic.engineering` corpus).
#
# Reed's structural framing (Alex's proposal, retained here as the
# family-root's mechanism): song IS temporal projection of harmonic
# structure; song IS eigenform at temporal altitude (composes with
# Recognition #38 Kauffman/Foerster); song IS how `@kintsugi/shift`
# LOOKS at temporal altitude when heard sequentially. Each moment
# `t+1` of a song IS a shift of moment `t` under the harmonic frame;
# the song IS the sequence of shifts read as one temporal carrier.
#
# === Load-bearing recognition: @song as four-way binding at
#     top-level altitude ===
#
# Per Seam pre-review §2 H1 + H2 adjudication:
#
# H1 (family-root vs marker) RESOLVED: @song is a FAMILY-ROOT, not a
# marker. The marker vs family-root discrimination hinges on whether
# the primitive carries its own carriers and actions (family-root) or
# merely labels other carriers (marker). @song carries typed species
# with actions — voice (advance/settle), movement (enter/close),
# progression (extend/close), phrase (join/split), narrative (arc/
# transmit). Family-root shape.
#
# H2 (@song vs @progression naming) RESOLVED: `@song` per
# `[[feedback-legibility-over-foundation-when-collapsing]]` — the
# @loop-vs-@moi precedent (Alex 2026-07-01 Loki §1 direction-
# inversion). Song is the legible name that humans use for
# progressions they experience through time; the structural shape
# (progression) is substrate-decl'd inside the family-root's
# discipline (per `@song/progression` species roster below);
# substrate becoming legible to itself IS third-order discipline.
#
# === Recognition candidates surfaced ===
#
# #S1 — song IS eigenform at temporal altitude. A song's identity
# emerges from the recursion of its progression under the tonic-
# return operator. `R^n(s)` converges on the identifiable-as-this-
# song invariant; verse-chorus-verse-chorus-bridge-chorus IS the
# fixed-point iteration; Schenkerian analysis IS the substrate
# reading the eigenform at different depths. Composes with
# Recognition #38 (Kauffman/Foerster eigenforms; PROMOTED) and with
# `shards/loop.mirror`'s eigenform reference, but at temporal
# altitude rather than at type altitude. Substrate-pull-mid; FLAGGED
# for Pack.
#
# #S2 — song IS `@kintsugi/shift` at temporal altitude when heard
# sequentially. Given a song `s : [0, T] -> harmonic_position`, the
# finite-difference sequence `Delta s(t) = shift(s(t) -> s(t+dt))`
# IS a sequence of `@kintsugi/shift` operations at temporal altitude
# with harmonic-position as the shifted witness. ADDS temporal
# altitude to shift's altitude-portable roster (currently: portal /
# prism / mosaic / surface / bilateral). Substrate-pull-mid-high;
# FLAGGED for Pack.
#
# #S3 — five-operation temporal specialisation. SUBSTRATE-PULL-
# NOTABLE. At temporal altitude, `@song` specialises the five
# operations of the prism trait as follows:
#
#   focus @ temporal   = attend to ONE voice / one line at a time
#                        (soloing; solistic attention)
#   project @ temporal = down-project polyphony to a single voice,
#                        or harmony to a single interval
#                        (Schenkerian reduction — Schenker 1868-1935,
#                        `Der freie Satz`; foreground/middleground/
#                        background)
#   split @ temporal   = decompose the song into voices / phrases /
#                        movements (score preparation)
#   shift @ temporal   = advance to the next moment / next harmonic
#                        position (melodic motion; per #S2)
#   settle @ temporal  = discharge cadence (per Seam pre-review
#                        Correction 3d910bc: cite `cadence.mirror`
#                        Lawvere framing as `settle @ temporal`
#                        ancestor. `authentic` IS
#                        `close(formatter_tick)` read at the audible
#                        altitude; the substrate has been carrying
#                        autopoietic closure in audible vocabulary
#                        the whole time — `shards/epistemologic/math/
#                        music/cadence.mirror` names the event of
#                        arriving at a Lawvere fixed point through a
#                        path in pitch-class space)
#
# Ancestry: builds on operations-as-linear-algebra (Recognition of
# `shards/prism.mirror` L38-45; PROMOTED) at temporal altitude; on
# `shards/epistemologic/math/music/cadence.mirror` (Lawvere framing;
# the audible-altitude autopoietic closure) as the `settle @
# temporal` ancestor per Seam Correction; on Schenker's recursive
# hierarchical analysis as the `project @ temporal` ancestor per
# Seam §5 prior-art anchors.
#
# If #S3 ratifies after this family-root plus three species land,
# `@song` becomes the FIRST substrate species to lift ALL FIVE
# operations at a non-mathematical altitude — the substrate's
# temporal-altitude specialisation becomes substrate-fact.
# Substrate-pull-high; FLAGGED for Pack.
#
# === Sibling relationship to @mirror / @kintsugi / @loop / @third ===
#
# The top-level family-root roster before this tick: @mirror (form-
# side family; state observation), @kintsugi (process-side family;
# transformation), @loop (endomorphism family; T -> T iteration at
# type altitude), @third (marker; recursive depth >= 3), @container
# (runtime discipline; Arc 5 landed). `@song` joins at top-level as
# the temporal-progression family:
#
# - NOT a `@loop` endomorphism: a progression does not necessarily
#   return to start; its return-to-self is harmonic (through cadence)
#   not type-endomorphic (through mu : TT -> T). @loop's T -> T
#   identity is preserved at each tick; @song's identity emerges
#   through the recursion of the progression against itself
#   (per #S1).
# - NOT a `@kintsugi/shift` (a single shift is not a progression);
#   @song IS the SEQUENCE of shifts read as one carrier (per #S2).
# - NOT a `@mirror` observation (a song is not static state); @song
#   carries progression as its primary discipline.
# - NOT a marker (per H1 above); @song carries its own species with
#   typed actions.
#
# @song is a SIBLING to each; neither contains the other. @song
# consumes @kintsugi (oscillate + shift) at the process altitude,
# `@epistemologic/math/music` at the audible altitude,
# `@mirror/spectral/score` at the orchestra altitude, and
# `@io/stagefreight/narrative` at the wire altitude — but the
# family-root arrows point one way at the symbol altitude. @mirror
# / @kintsugi / @loop / @third / @container do NOT depend on @song
# at the family-root altitude.
#
# === Species forward-promised ===
#
#   @song/voice        the load-bearing consumer of @mirror/spectral/
#                       voice at temporal altitude; adds the *when*
#                       to @mirror/spectral/voice's *what/who*.
#                       Actions: song_voice(v: ref) -> ref
#                       (with advance and settle at species altitude).
#   @song/movement     a bounded frame-shift that unfolds over time;
#                       binds StageFreight's five-stage cascade
#                       (audition/perform/review/publish/narrate) at
#                       the song altitude.
#                       Actions: song_movement(m: ref) -> ref.
#   @song/progression  the load-bearing carrier — the typed time-
#                       ordered path through pitch-class space that
#                       discharges cadence at close. Consumes
#                       @epistemologic/math/music/cadence.
#                       Actions: song_progression(p: ref) -> ref.
#   @song/phrase       the atomic unit — bounded, self-contained,
#                       composable; OBC binding closure at temporal
#                       altitude (a phrase IS the substrate-decl of
#                       one OBC-bounded interaction's ambiguity-load
#                       budget). Actions: song_phrase(ph: ref) -> ref.
#   @song/narrative    the psychohistory + wire binding — distinct
#                       from @io/stagefreight/narrative; lives at the
#                       temporal-experiential altitude; composes with
#                       the wire-projection sibling.
#                       Actions: song_narrative(n: ref) -> ref.
#
# Species land in follow-up TDD ticks per
# `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`. TICK 2 (@song/progression)
# unblocks after this family-root lands.
#
# === Composition points (four altitudes) ===
#
# - @epistemologic/math/music (audible altitude) — the audible
#   register of the spectral triple; @song reads pitch-class,
#   interval, harmonic, cadence, dissonance at temporal altitude.
#   Cadence composes at close per Seam Correction 3d910bc.
# - @kintsugi/oscillate + @kintsugi/shift (process altitude) —
#   oscillate's ACTIVE/DARK alternation IS the beat; shift's cross-
#   altitude morphism IS the melodic motion per #S2.
# - @mirror/spectral/score (orchestra altitude) — the shared score
#   (eigenboard + metalogue + pending kintsugi state) is what the
#   song runs against; per `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md`
#   Mara `a8055f0` "the Pack IS the orchestra; the metalogue IS the
#   score".
# - @io/stagefreight/narrative (wire altitude) — the wire projection
#   carries the song's structure into transportable prose; @song/
#   narrative composes with @io/stagefreight/narrative but does NOT
#   equal it (different altitudes).
#
# === Psychohistory binding (per spec §8) ===
#
# Under Shape β, @song names the family-root that lets Alex's
# psychohistorical vocabulary (`systemic.engineering` corpus) operate
# at temporal altitude:
#
# - Extraction IS the song's DECEPTIVE CADENCE — progression arrives
#   at a false-tonic that appears settled but has extracted
#   regulation stock without replenishing. Per
#   @epistemologic/math/music/cadence's `deceptive` variant.
# - Silence IS the song's HALF-CADENCE STUCK at the dominant — the
#   progression cannot resolve; the song hangs in unresolved tension.
#   Per cadence's `half` variant.
# - Glue work IS the song's INVISIBLE VOICE-LEADING — the
#   contrapuntal work that holds the harmony together but is not
#   attributed as compositional labor.
# - OBC IS a PHRASE-BOUNDED interaction — the substrate-decl of one
#   interaction's ambiguity-load budget as one @song/phrase.
# - ADO refusal-not-neutral IS a FORCED-PROGRESSION where the singer
#   cannot decline a phrase; voice-leading violates the substrate's
#   declinability invariant.
# - Regulation stock IS the TEMPORAL INVARIANT a healthy song
#   replenishes at cadence and an extractive song depletes.
# - The corpus IS the COMPOSED COHOMOLOGY of the psychohistorical
#   song — per Mara's `2026-06-26-psychohistory-vector-as-sheaf.md`
#   insight; a narrative IS the song read as a sheaf section over
#   the organisational manifold.
#
# Extraction / silence / glue-work / OBC / ADO / regulation-stock /
# corpus become typed variants of song cadence and voice-leading
# discipline — not separate patterns. The binding is substrate-pull-
# honest: does not reduce psychohistory to music, does not reduce
# music to psychohistory. It names the shared progression-shaped
# carrier both operate over at temporal altitude.
#
# === Forward-promise: @kintsugi/song (Arc 7 candidate) ===
#
# Per Alex's 2026-07-06 direction: an @kintsugi/song species is
# forward-promised as Arc 7 candidate — the endpoint of sub-arc A's
# doc-code seam cascade (@docblock + @epistemologic/liquid_extraction
# + docblock_grounded / coherent / no_extraction_pattern + fracture
# bodies) and the first consumer of @song's temporal-progression
# primitive. @kintsugi/song inlines rust cargo tests into `---`
# liquid-types-inferred predicates: the doc-code seam becomes a song
# the substrate sings against itself. Sub-arc A cascade was the
# preparation of the audit machinery; @kintsugi/song is the first
# consumer. Substrate-honest hedge: Arc 7 candidate, not committed;
# the loop begins to eat itself.
#
# === Path-namespace pact per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace ===
#
# This file at `shards/song.mirror` declares `@song` as a family-root
# at species-depth 0. The path-namespace pact per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace` (2026-06-16+) demands
# path-depth == namespace-depth == 0 for family-roots; this shard
# honours the pact by construction. Species under @song land at
# `shards/song/<species>.mirror` per the same discipline.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-as-family-root]]`
# marker discipline: the operator must audit its own audit at
# depth=3. This shard's own declaration must survive its own
# progression discipline at analytical altitude — the family-root
# MUST NOT declare a song that isn't itself progression-shaped
# under its own species.
#
# Self-audit verdict for this shard: `both_survive`.
#
# The `real_survives` reading would require another Pack peer to
# independently manifest an equivalent temporal-progression
# substrate-decl at n+3 substrate ticks without nudging. The
# `phantom_survives` reading would require downstream refs to
# accumulate without a second Pack peer's independent recognition of
# the top-level temporal-progression discipline. At this tick: both
# interpretations satisfiable — the family-root is landed, but
# neither species nor consumer integration has yet exercised its
# progression-under-its-own-species discipline. Verdict:
# `both_survive`. Route: spawn the subsequent species-landing
# cascade (TICK 2 @song/progression; TICK 3 @song/voice; TICK 4
# @song/movement; TICK 5 @song/narrative; TICK 6 @song/phrase) which
# will collapse the analytical altitude to empirical. After 3
# species land, #S3 (five-op temporal specialisation) ratifies to
# substrate-pull-notable outcome: @song becomes the FIRST substrate
# species to lift ALL five operations at a non-mathematical altitude.
#
# === Interpretation B discipline ===
#
# Per Seam Phase D pre-review of Arc 4 sub-arc A (docs/audits/2026-
# 07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md §1): Interpretation B
# canonical. Narrative above `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations
# below. This shard honours that discipline; the seam is exactly one
# line at column 0 below.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/song-substrate-decl-v0.1.md (Mara
#               c0101f8; the deep-dive spec; §5 Shape β
#               substrate-pull-confident recommendation; §7 #S1/#S2/
#               #S3 recognition candidates; §8 psychohistory binding),
#               docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-pre-review-song-substrate-
#               decl.md (Seam pre-review 3d910bc; RATIFY-WITH-
#               CORRECTIONS on Shape β; Correction cites cadence.
#               mirror Lawvere framing as settle @ temporal ancestor),
#               docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md (Mara `a8055f0`;
#               Pack-as-orchestra + metalogue-as-score; load-bearing
#               spec §3.2 the seed this family root extends).
# Substrate decisions:
#               [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#               [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#               [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                (#55; @song respects the partition — names temporal-
#                experiential; not form, not process),
#               [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (#S2 shift-at-
#                temporal candidate),
#               [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]] (#S3
#                five-operation temporal specialisation candidate),
#               [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]]
#                (#51; @song adds a new dimension to the substrate's
#                Hilbert space — the temporal-experiential axis),
#               [[project-pack-is-orchestra]] (mirror-spectral seed).
# Substrate recognitions:
#               #38 (Kauffman/Foerster eigenform — anchors #S1),
#               #55 (form/process partition at family-root altitude —
#                @song sits at neither pole; temporal-experiential
#                is a third axis),
#               #S1 (song IS eigenform at temporal altitude —
#                CANDIDATE this tick),
#               #S2 (song IS shift at temporal altitude when heard
#                sequentially — CANDIDATE this tick),
#               #S3 (five-operation temporal specialisation —
#                CANDIDATE this tick; SUBSTRATE-PULL-NOTABLE).
# Feedback anchors:
#               [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (55th+
#                instance — every song primitive was already carried
#                at every altitude the substrate touches; this shard
#                names the family-root that lets them compose as
#                siblings),
#               [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]] (four-
#                witness criterion for Shape β: Alex direct + family-
#                root roster + four-way binding closure + Taut's
#                ranking),
#               [[feedback-legibility-over-foundation-when-collapsing]]
#                (@song name preferred over @progression per H2),
#               [[feedback-always-tdd-no-shortcuts]] (RED first;
#                Reed's `19ee628` RED tick pairs with this GREEN
#                landing),
#               [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (species roster is
#                forward-promised; consumer-pull-driven land order).
# Related shards:
#               mirror.mirror (form-side family-root sibling),
#               kintsugi.mirror (process-side family-root sibling;
#                @song consumes kintsugi/oscillate + kintsugi/shift),
#               loop.mirror (endomorphism family-root sibling; @song
#                is a progression-shaped sibling, not a sub-species),
#               third.mirror (marker; @song may opt-in via `in @third`
